==================== Input ====================
// The content gate reads key presence, never the value.
//
// Upstream tests `if (jsonObj.openapi)`, so this root stays unordered there. Here it is an OpenAPI
// document and the root is reordered, which is the divergence the crate docs record: a document
// that names a version field without filling it in is still an OpenAPI document.
//
// JSON has one root per file, so the other falsy spellings (`0`, `false`, `null`) are covered by
// `../../../yaml/openapi/falsy-openapi-value.yaml`; the gate is the same key-presence test in both
// backends. `info` is written after `paths` so a reordered root is visible in the output.
{
  "openapi": "",
  "paths": {
    "/p": {
      "get": {
        "responses": {}
      }
    }
  },
  "info": {
    "title": "empty string"
  }
}

